+# Changes
+
+## Round 1
+
+Addresses `REVIEW.md` round 0 (held-out suite: 11 failures in two groups).
+
+- `src/layer.mjs`: a key whose value in `over` is `undefined` is now treated as not given, at any depth. It leaves base's value alone (an object stays, as a copy), and a key only `over` has with `undefined` does not appear in the result. Fixes the whole "undefined" group (4 cases). This replaces the round 0 decision that `undefined` replaces the base value.
+- `src/layer.mjs`: `copy` now throws a `TypeError` for any value that is not plain data (functions, symbols, Maps, Sets, class instances), wherever it sits: top-level values, nested objects, inside arrays, in `base` or in `over`. Fixes the whole "not plain data" group (7 cases). This replaces the round 0 decision that such values are kept by reference, so the "shares nothing" promise (checklist 4) now holds for every value that can be in a result.
+- `tests/layer.test.mjs`: added a test for each case in the "undefined" group and a test refusing function, Map, Set, class instance and symbol at each position named in the findings (value in `over`, value in `base`, inside an array, deep in either argument).
+- `CHANGELOG.md`: line updated to mention the new behaviour.
+
+Unchanged decisions from round 0:
+- Plain object means prototype is `Object.prototype` or `null`. Arrays, Dates, Maps, class instances and functions are not plain, so they throw as arguments.
+- Both inputs are deep-copied first (plain objects, arrays, Dates), then merged, so nothing is mutated and nothing is shared.
+- `__proto__`, `constructor` and `prototype` keys are dropped at every depth, including inside arrays. Every rebuilt object is an ordinary `{}`.
+- Circular structures throw a `TypeError`.
+- Dates nested in settings are still accepted and copied (the findings do not name them).
+- `undefined` as an array element, or as a value in `base`, is kept as is; only object keys in `over` are treated as not given.
